  "_fix_note": "E2 FIX (D-315). Two defects in v1, both silent. (a) If CHECKLIST MAP has no row for a visa type that IS in the router list, module 3 returns zero bundles, modules 4 and 5 never run, column Y stays empty and the row re-matches the trigger on EVERY run, forever. limit=5, so five such rows permanently starve M4. Visa 190 is in the router; the CHECKLIST MAP setup script has 36 rows and no 190 entry, so this was live. (b) If the copy succeeded but module 5 failed, Y also stayed empty and M4 re-copied the same checklist on every run, piling duplicates into the client folder. v2 stamps Y BEFORE the lookup, so the row always leaves the queue; module 5 overwrites the stamp with the real filename on success. Cost: +1 op per filed row. Also excludes rows M3 flagged NEEDS ROUTING. Only exist/notexist/text:equal/text:notequal are used (D-255)."
